-- title:
--   Both chart derivative ideals have explicit finite jet generators and degrees
-- statement:
--   For each of the two Weierstrass charts and every natural number T, the order-T differential prolongation of the ideal (F_c, Q_c) is exactly the ideal generated by
--
--   F_c, Q_c, D_c Q_c, ..., D_c^T Q_c.
--
--   Thus the family has T+2 entries (which need not be distinct or minimal). If Q is bihomogeneous of degrees (m,n) in its first two and last five variables, respectively, every displayed generator has total degree at most max(3, m+2n+T).
--
--   This is equality of ideals, preserving scheme multiplicities and localized quotient lengths. It is stronger than equality of zero sets or radicals. The degree estimate for individual normalized jets was already established in the earlier chart-jet work; the new step combines it with a proof that these jets generate the entire derivative ideal of the explicit cubic-plus-Q base. The estimate grows with T and does not establish A.1's uniform degree budget.
-- source:
--   Philippon (1986), Lemmes de zeros dans les groupes algebriques commutatifs, Bull. Soc. Math. France 114, 355-383, section 5, pp. 380-382: derivative and translation ideals in the zero-estimate argument. https://www.numdam.org/item/10.24033/bsmf.2060.pdf. Senthil Kumar K (2026), Appendix A, Theorem A.2. https://doi.org/10.1017/S001309152610145X. The new algebraic step proves that each order-T prolongation of the explicit cubic-plus-Q chart base is generated by the cubic and the normalized Q jets through order T, preserving exact ideals and lengths. The individual jet-degree bounds were already available and are reused. The common total-degree bound max(3,m+2*n+T) depends on T; it does not prove the uniform total multiplicity budget. Geometric locus selection, coset/component control and the uniform degree estimate remain Open.

import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassEllipticZeta_FiniteChartJets

open TranscendenceTheory WeierstrassEllipticZeta

theorem WeierstrassEllipticZeta.elliptic_chart_finite_jet_generators
    (L : PeriodPair) (Q : MvPolynomial (Fin 7) ℂ) (c : Fin 2) (T : ℕ) :
    differentialProlongation (extensionChartDerivation L.g₂ L.g₃ c)
      (extensionCubicChartBaseIdeal L Q c) T = extensionChartJetIdeal L Q c T ∧
    ∀ m n : ℕ,
      (∀ d ∈ Q.support, d 0 + d 1 = m ∧ d 2 + d 3 + d 4 + d 5 + d 6 = n) →
      ∀ j : Fin (T + 2),
        (extensionChartJetGenerator L Q c T j).totalDegree ≤ max 3 (m + 2 * n + T) := by sorry
